  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Wednesday)\n\nUpper pattern will become relatively quiet through Sunday, as \nmodels show a very weak and broad scale subtle troughing over \nNevada and most of central and southern California. Just to the \nnorthwest of this trough, a weak shallow upper level shortwave \nridge will set up over northern California, and SE Oregon. This \nflow setup looks to keep Nevada dry for the next several days, \nhowever with the westerly Jet just to the north, models have \ntrended higher with the winds as the pressure gradient over \nnorthern Nevada has tightened over recent runs. So will need to \nwatch for possible fire weather issues as westerly winds of 10 MPH\nto 20 MPH with gusts up to 35 MPH possible over northern Humboldt\nand Elko counties through Saturday. Elsewhere winds will be \nlighter out of the W-SW at 5 to 15 MPH with gusts up to 25 MPH \npossible. Monday, models show a northern stream upper level trough\nmoving through Nevada, models have come into better agreement \nwith this system as both the GFS and ECMWF show a fast moving \nsystem. Another change is that models are showing the potential of\nsome light isolated showers accompanying trough passage Monday \nafternoon and evening, with the trough exiting east Monday night. \nTuesday and Wednesday ridging returns bringing another period of \nquiet weather conditions back to the Silver State. Temperature \nwise a quick warming trend will last through Thursday as highs \npeak in the mid to upper 80s. Friday through Monday a cooling \ntrend will see temperatures falling into the mid 70s for highs. \nLows will range in the mid to upper 40s for the first half of the \nforecast period, cooling into the mid to upper 30s by middle of \nnext week.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n \n\nThere is high confidence in a much drier pattern lasting through \nMonday of next week.\n\nThere is low confidence in the potential for a 10% to 20% chance \nfor isolated showers across northern Nevada as an upper trough \npasses through Monday of next week.\n\nThere is moderate to high confidence in the return of upper level\nridging for the middle of next week restoring quiet and dry \npattern over Nevada.",
